Design priority: normal runtime behavior, maintainability and elimination of duplicated publication/refresh code determine the API. This audit records compatibility obligations, not a mandate for lifecycle infrastructure. Shutdown and /exit are secondary exceptional paths to address with minimal local remedies where necessary; do not use hypothetical cleanup issues to drive the ordinary runtime design.

Determine ordering responsibilities hidden in snapshot construction/application and submission completion. Trace apply_runtime_state_snapshot and presentation-transition wrappers, RuntimeActiveRunController, RuntimeSubmitController, worker results, Session replacement/detached states and shutdown. Cover new/clear/resume/switch/fork/branch, reloads, queued submissions and delayed completions. Establish each worker/result/event identity before and after transitions and where stale work is rejected.

Inventory effects on grants, prompt/attachment authority, active-agent selection, directories/workspace root, drafts/stash, transcript replacement, search/selection/scroll, overview, selectors, subagent views, cancellation and outstanding callbacks. Trace the actual selected-agent owner and selection writers through next-Enter submission rather than inferring authority from labels. Separate backend-affecting visible facts published through UnlockedData from UI-only effects owned in tui-specific files on the tui-thread without locks/UnlockedData. Draft text stays exclusively frontend-owned until string submission. Establish which effects require ordered processing rather than latest-value observation. Preserve existing history/streaming transition and stale-result handling as an explicit deferred exception; no new journal or history redesign. Specify only needed identity/revision, notification-lifetime, cancellation/join and backend lock-order contracts for migrated facts and local consequences.

Trace the two /exit statistics publications, separating required final usage/persistence from redundant presentation-triggered computation. Produce a lifecycle artifact with contents, concrete call chains and deterministic tests for rapid transitions, old-session completions, failed transitions, interaction cancellation and shutdown. State uncertainties as investigation requirements. This is design evidence only; do not move quit checks, remove cleanup or change behavior while auditing.
